@startuml mppdp5-software-factory-gates
title mppdp5 — Software Factory / Quality Gates
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

[*] --> PRD
state "Requirements\n(PRD)" as PRD
state "Design\n(UML + Ontology + ADR)" as Design
state "Implementation\n(GitHub Issue / PR)" as Build
state "Verification\n(Tests + Contracts)" as Test
state "Deploy" as Deploy
state "Observe" as Observe
state "Kaizen\n(continuous improvement)" as Kaizen

PRD --> G1 : requirements ready
state "GATE-REQUIREMENTS-001" as G1 <<choice>>
G1 --> Design : pass
G1 --> PRD : fail / revise

Design --> G2 : design ready
state "GATE-DESIGN-001" as G2 <<choice>>
G2 --> Build : pass
G2 --> Design : fail / revise

Build --> G3 : implementation ready
state "GATE-IMPLEMENTATION-001" as G3 <<choice>>
G3 --> Test : pass
G3 --> Build : fail / revise

Test --> G4 : checks complete
state "GATE-TEST-001" as G4 <<choice>>
G4 --> Deploy : pass
G4 --> Build : fail / fix

Deploy --> Observe
Observe --> Kaizen
Kaizen --> PRD : new requirements / improvement

note bottom of Build
  Kanban pull flow:
  respect WIP limits,
  make blocked work visible,
  start only when downstream
  review/test capacity exists.
end note

note bottom of Test
  Quality is built in.
  Failed checks must not
  move downstream.
end note

note bottom of Observe
  Failures are andon signals.
  Turn recurring defects into
  traceable improvement issues.
end note
@enduml
